1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,240
They analyze on the slow queries, and the problem is a missing composite index on the

2
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:08,880
orders table, on customer ID, and created that.

3
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,840
Someone dropped it during the schema migration with Alembic.

4
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:14,480
Ouch!

5
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:16,220
Is there a fix ready?

6
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:17,900
Yes.

7
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:23,880
I wrote a new migration that recreates the index concurrently, so it will not lock the

8
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:24,560
SQL.

9
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:32,440
I also added a check in our CI pipeline, using pgstat statements, so we get an alert in Datadog

10
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,620
if any query goes above 200 milliseconds.

11
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,240
That's really helpful.

12
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,540
From the product side, customers definitely noticed.

13
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:49,260
We had 11 support tickets about slow checkout in the last week, and our NPS score dropped

14
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:50,660
by 3 points.

15
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:53,540
Thanks, Aisha.

16
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:57,260
Okay, item 3, the Q3OKRs.

17
00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:59,540
Aisha, can you give us the summary?
